  "description": "T-4622: which function the countA and count custom subtotals of a pivot field compute, and how Excel labels each line. Data!A1:F10 has Region, Product and four value fields over nine records: East A 10, East A text abc, East B blank, East B #N/A, East B 5, West A 7, West B text x, West B TRUE, West B 3 (Val); Clean is Val with the #N/A replaced by 2. So East has 5 records, 4 non-blank Val values (COUNTA) and 2 numbers (COUNT); West has 4 records, 4 non-blank and 2 numbers; Clean East has 4 non-blank and 3 numbers. ErrFirst and ErrLast hold Val's East values reordered with the #N/A first (East A row 2: #N/A, 10, abc, blank, 5) and last (10, abc, blank, 5, #N/A in row 6, East B), West as Val, to tell whether an error ends the subtotal's count in record order or per inner item. Each sheet is one tabular builder-v2 pivot, rows Region (outer, custom subtotals, no default) and Product. CA: countA alone, Sum of Val. CN: count alone, Sum of Val. B1: countA and count, Sum of Val. B2: both, Sum of Clean (no error). B3: both, Count of Val (whether the subtotal function or the data field's aggregate wins). B4 and B5: both, Sum of ErrFirst and Sum of ErrLast. Pivot cells are in the sidecar's `pivots` section; Q!A1 makes the case scored.",
